{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y2nDK1YqvyS4gciysrYy8A","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 'Task-dependent convergence 在 LAMBADA + StoryCloze 两个独立 retrieval\n2\t  benchmark 上成立\n3\t\n4\t  （均 ρ=-1.0, two-tailed exact permutation p=0.017）。统计策略：exp-001 taxonomy 先于\n5\t\n6\t  exp-011 建立 retrieval-task subset（m=5）作为 pre-specified correction scope——\n7\t\n8\t  BH-FDR 保留 2 个 benchmark（adj_p=0.042），Bonferroni 在 confirmatory subset（m=3）\n9\t\n10\t  borderline 保留 1 个（adj_p=0.050）。Full m=9 correction 下无 benchmark 显著——诚实报告。\n11\t\n12\t  Per-example divergence 在 4 个架构上量化（+Mamba2-hybrid, exp-005），Jaccard 0.05-0.09。\n13\t\n14\t  exp-003 两层 negative（surface features + perplexity 均不预测 within-arch helped/hurt）\n15\t\n16\t  排除 trivial explanations；cross-arch KW（p=0.0005）确认 structured specificity。\n17\t\n18\t  Attention pattern 提供中等描述性关联（mean r=0.36, exp-004）。\n19\t\n20\t  340M rebound 有 capacity bottleneck 解释（rebound samples 73% 在 top difficulty quartile）。\n21\t\n22\t  W1 降级为 addressed；W4 通过第 4 架构 + per-example 独立贡献缓解。目标 EMNLP Main。\n23\t\n24\t  '\n25\timagined_experiments:\n26\t- name: Task-specificity characterization of equalizer effect\n27\t  plan_id: exp-001\n28\t  description: 6 benchmark 跨架构 std 轨迹 + exact permutation Spearman + 任务分类体系（已完成，actual\n29\t    results）\n30\t  expected_results:\n31\t    LAMBADA_rho: -1.0\n32\t    LAMBADA_p_two_tailed: 0.017\n33\t    LAMBADA_std_pure: 0.024\n34\t    LAMBADA_std_h3_1: 0.005\n35\t    LAMBADA_std_reduction_pct: 79\n36\t    HellaSwag_rho: 0.3\n37\t    ARC_C_rho: 0.6\n38\t    Winogrande_rho: 0.1\n39\t    ARC_Easy_rho: -0.7\n40\t    ARC_Easy_p: 0.233\n41\t    MMLU_rho: -0.7\n42\t    MMLU_p: 0.233\n43\t    significant_count: 1/6\n44\t    taxonomy:\n45\t      retrieval_dependent:\n46\t      - LAMBADA\n47\t      mixed:\n48\t      - ARC-Easy\n49\t      - MMLU\n50\t      reasoning_dependent:\n51\t      - HellaSwag\n52\t      - ARC-C\n53\t      - Winogrande\n54\t  result_rationale: '已完成实验的实际结果。Best 档解读的关键：taxonomy 是 PREDICTIVE framework，不是 post-hoc\n55\t    rationalization。\n56\t\n57\t    LAMBADA（last-word prediction from passage）依赖 attention 的 copy/induction-head retrieval\n58\t    mechanism——\n59\t\n60\t    所有架构的 attention 都学会类似的 context retrieval → 性能趋同。\n61\t\n62\t    Reasoning 任务（HellaSwag/ARC-C/Winogrande）依赖 recurrent state 的 compositional inference，\n63\t\n64\t    attention 不系统性改变这一计算 → ρ ≈ 0 或正值。\n65\t\n66\t    Mixed 类（ARC-Easy ρ=-0.7, MMLU ρ=-0.7）有 factual retrieval 成分但不纯粹 → suggestive trend。\n67\t\n68\t    核心价值：taxonomy 为 exp-011 提供了 a priori prediction——高 retrieval demand 的新 benchmark\n69\t\n70\t    应显示 convergence——使 exp-011 从 fishing expedition 变为 hypothesis-driven confirmatory\n71\t    test。\n72\t\n73\t    '\n74\t  tables:\n75\t  - 'Table 1: Cross-architecture convergence by benchmark (ρ, exact permutation p,\n76\t    taxonomy)'\n77\t  figures_description:\n78\t  - 'Fig 1a: Cross-arch std vs attention ratio (5 points × 6 benchmarks), color-coded\n79\t    by taxonomy'\n80\t  analysis: 'Taxonomy 成立。ρ 值沿 retrieval demand gradient 单调递减：\n81\t\n82\t    LAMBADA(-1.0) > ARC-Easy/MMLU(-0.7) > ARC-C(0.6)/HellaSwag(0.3)/Winogrande(0.1)。\n83\t\n84\t    这个 gradient 本身是一个 finding：convergence strength 是 retrieval demand 的函数。\n85\t\n86\t    '\n87\t- name: Multi-benchmark per-example analysis\n88\t  plan_id: exp-002\n89\t  description: HellaSwag/ARC-Easy/ARC-Challenge 收集 --log_samples 数据（10×340M + 3×1.3B），验证\n90\t    per-example task-specificity\n91\t  expected_results:\n92\t    n_models_evaluated: 13\n93\t    gpu_hours_used: 18\n94\t    LAMBADA_jaccard_mean: 0.07\n95\t    ARC_Easy_jaccard_mean: 0.09\n96\t    ARC_Challenge_jaccard_mean: 0.14\n97\t    HellaSwag_jaccard_mean: 0.16\n98\t    LAMBADA_mean_effect_magnitude: 0.055\n99\t    ARC_Easy_mean_effect_magnitude: 0.038\n100\t    ARC_Challenge_mean_effect_magnitude: 0.025\n101\t    HellaSwag_mean_effect_magnitude: 0.02\n102\t    task_specificity_per_example_confirmed: true\n103\t    jaccard_retrieval_demand_correlation: -0.92\n104\t  result_rationale: 'LAMBADA 低 Jaccard（0.07）：不同架构的 attention 用不同 retrieval strategy（copy-head\n105\t    vs\n106\t\n107\t    induction-head vs local-window）rescue 不同的 sample——每种 recurrence bias 与 attention\n108\t    的\n109\t\n110\t    互补方式不同，导致 \"被 rescue 的 sample 集合\" 高度 architecture-specific。\n111\t\n112\t    HellaSwag 高 Jaccard（0.16）：reasoning 任务上 attention 的 per-example 效应缺乏 systematic\n113\t    pattern，\n114\t\n115\t    帮助/伤害更接近随机重排。随机集合的 expected Jaccard 高于 structured 集合——这正是\n116\t\n117\t    \"reasoning 任务无 systematic convergence\" 在 per-example 层面的 signature。\n118\t\n119\t    |effect| gradient（LAMBADA 0.055 > ARC-E 0.038 > ARC-C 0.025 > HellaSwag 0.020）\n120\t\n121\t    与 Jaccard gradient 一致：retrieval 任务上 attention 效应更强且更 structured。\n122\t\n123\t    Combined Jaccard-retrieval demand correlation（ρ=-0.92）量化了 dose-response 关系。\n124\t\n125\t    '\n126\t  tables:\n127\t  - 'Table 2: Per-example divergence metrics by benchmark (Jaccard, |effect|, n_helped,\n128\t    n_hurt)'\n129\t  figures_description:\n130\t  - 'Fig 3: Jaccard heatmap — architecture pair × benchmark; LAMBADA 列深蓝，reasoning\n131\t    列浅色'\n132\t  - 'Fig 4: Per-example effect maps — ARC-Easy (structured blocks) vs HellaSwag (salt-and-pepper)'\n133\t  analysis: 'Per-example 数据将 task-specificity 从 aggregate-only 提升为 multi-level validation。\n134\t\n135\t    Jaccard gradient 是 exp-001 taxonomy 在 per-example 层面的独立确认。\n136\t\n137\t    HellaSwag per-example non-convergence 排除了 \"hidden convergence masked by aggregate\n138\t    noise\"。\n139\t\n140\t    '\n141\t- name: Helped/hurt sample characterization\n142\t  plan_id: exp-003\n143\t  description: Surface features（Phase 1）+ baseline perplexity（Phase 2）分析（两 phase 均已完成，actual\n144\t    results）\n145\t  expected_results:\n146\t    within_arch_surface_features_any_significant: false\n147\t    RetNet_context_length_p: 0.012\n148\t    RetNet_context_length_r: -0.096\n149\t    RetNet_unique_tokens_p: 0.009\n150\t    RetNet_unique_tokens_r: -0.099\n151\t    GDN_all_p_values_gt: 0.5\n152\t    HGRN2_all_p_values_gt: 0.2\n153\t    cross_arch_surface_difference: not_significant\n154\t    within_arch_perplexity_significant: false\n155\t    GDN_ppl_U: 148410\n156\t    GDN_ppl_p: 0.209\n157\t    GDN_ppl_r_rb: -0.045\n158\t    RetNet_ppl_p: 0.659\n159\t    RetNet_ppl_r_rb: -0.017\n160\t    HGRN2_ppl_p: 0.248\n161\t    HGRN2_ppl_r_rb: -0.044\n162\t    cross_arch_hurt_KW_p: 0.0005\n163\t    cross_arch_helped_KW_p: 0.02\n164\t  result_rationale: 'Best 档解读：两层 negative 是 asset 而非 liability。\n165\t\n166\t    Phase 1 negative：token frequency、context length、lexical diversity 不预测 helped/hurt\n167\t    →\n168\t\n169\t    排除 \"attention 只帮长句子\" 或 \"只帮罕见词\" 等 trivial explanation。\n170\t\n171\t    Phase 2 negative：baseline perplexity 也不预测（r_rb ≈ -0.04, p > 0.2 三架构均如此）→\n172\t\n173\t    排除最自然的 first-order hypothesis \"attention rescues uncertain samples\"。\n174\t\n175\t    这两层 negative 共同确立：per-example effect 不由 sample 的固有属性或 baseline difficulty 驱动，\n176\t\n177\t    而由 architecture-attention 交互的 higher-order structure 驱动。\n178\t\n179\t    Cross-arch KW 显著（hurt p=0.0005）是 KEY positive result：\n180\t\n181\t    不同架构 hurt 的 sample 有系统性不同的 baseline difficulty profile。\n182\t\n183\t    GDN hurt mean ppl=3.34, RetNet=3.42, HGRN2=3.35——差异虽不大但统计显著，\n184\t\n185\t    因为 n 大（462-615 per architecture）。\n186\t\n187\t    叙事：underspecification 不是 trivially predictable（within-arch negative）但也不是 random\n188\t    noise\n189\t\n190\t    （cross-arch structured）。这是 underspecification 文献中的 characteristic signature。\n191\t\n192\t    '\n193\t  tables:\n194\t  - 'Table 3a: Within-arch tests — surface features (all NS) + perplexity (all NS)'\n195\t  - 'Table 3b: Cross-arch Kruskal-Wallis — hurt KW p=0.0005, helped KW p=0.020'\n196\t  figures_description:\n197\t  - 'Fig 5: Violin plot — hurt sample baseline perplexity per architecture (3 distributions,\n198\t    KW p=0.0005)'\n199\t  analysis: '负面结果的叙事价值在 best 档下充分发挥：两层 negative + cross-arch positive\n200\t\n201\t    构成 \"opaque within, structured across\" 的完整 characterization。\n202\t\n203\t    为 exp-004 的 attention analysis 设定了 expectation：mechanism 不在 sample-level features，\n204\t\n205\t    而在 model-sample 交互的 attention dynamics。\n206\t\n207\t    '\n208\t- name: Attention weight extraction and visualization\n209\t  plan_id: exp-004\n210\t  description: 提取 GDN/RetNet/HGRN2 h3-1 的 attention weights，分析 attention pattern 与\n211\t    per-example effect 关联\n212\t  expected_results:\n213\t    n_models_analyzed: 3\n214\t    GDN_attn_concentration_effect_r: 0.37\n215\t    GDN_attn_concentration_effect_p: 0.004\n216\t    RetNet_attn_concentration_effect_r: 0.4\n217\t    RetNet_attn_concentration_effect_p: 0.001\n218\t    HGRN2_attn_concentration_effect_r: 0.31\n219\t    HGRN2_attn_concentration_effect_p: 0.011\n220\t    mean_r_across_archs: 0.36\n221\t    n_archs_with_r_gt_0_3: 3\n222\t    cross_arch_attn_pattern_cosine_sim: 0.21\n223\t    helped_attn_entropy_lower_than_hurt: true\n224\t    GDN_modal_attn_distance: 3-8 tokens (compensating delta-rule recent-context decay)\n225\t    RetNet_modal_attn_distance: 8-20 tokens (compensating exponential mid-range decay)\n226\t    HGRN2_modal_attn_distance: 5-15 tokens (variable, hierarchical gate-dependent)\n227\t    gpu_hours_used: 3.5\n228\t  result_rationale: 'Attention concentration（低 entropy）与 per-example positive effect\n229\t    的中等相关（mean r=0.36）\n230\t\n231\t    来源于两个 complementary mechanism：\n232\t\n233\t    (1) Helped samples：attention 成功定位 recurrent state 缺失的信息位置\n234\t\n235\t    （LAMBADA → target word 的 semantic antecedent），产生集中的 attention pattern（低 entropy）。\n236\t\n237\t    (2) Hurt samples：recurrent state 已充分编码必要信息，attention 的额外 computation 分散\n238\t\n239\t    probability mass（高 entropy, diffuse attention），反而干扰。\n240\t\n241\t    r ≈ 0.36 而非更高（<0.5）有三个原因：\n242\t\n243\t    (a) multi-head aggregation 是 coarse proxy——不同 head 有不同 role；\n244\t\n245\t    (b) 部分 concentrated-but-wrong（attention 聚焦错误位置 → still hurt）；\n246\t\n247\t    (c) 部分 diffuse-but-helpful（weak signal > no signal when recurrent state 很弱）。\n248\t\n249\t    Cross-arch attention similarity 低（cosine 0.21）直接解释低 Jaccard：\n250\t\n251\t    GDN attention 补偿 delta-rule 的近距离衰减（聚焦 3-8 tokens），\n252\t\n253\t    RetNet 补偿 exponential 的中距离衰减（8-20 tokens），\n254\t\n255\t    HGRN2 补偿 hierarchical gate 的不规则 retention（5-15, variable）。\n256\t\n257\t    关键：这是 DESCRIPTIVE correlation。exp-003 Phase 2 的 negative perplexity result 意味着\n258\t\n259\t    attention pattern 不能还原为 \"rescue uncertain tokens\"——它是 attention-recurrence 交互的\n260\t\n261\t    emergent property，不可从 sample 属性预测。避免 mechanistic overclaiming（W3）。\n262\t\n263\t    '\n264\t  tables:\n265\t  - 'Table 4: Attention entropy vs per-example effect (per architecture, Mann-Whitney\n266\t    + rank-biserial r)'\n267\t  - 'Table 5: Attention focus distance comparison across architectures'\n268\t  figures_description:\n269\t  - 'Fig 6: Attention heatmaps — 3 archs × 3 sample types (helped-by-all, helped-by-one,\n270\t    hurt-by-all)'\n271\t  - 'Fig 7: Scatter — attention entropy vs effect magnitude, 3 colors for 3 architectures,\n272\t    negative trend'\n273\t  analysis: 'r=0.36 满足 >0.3 threshold，支持 \"partial descriptive account\"。\n274\t\n275\t    不同架构的不同 dominant pattern 给读者 intuitive mental model for architecture-specificity。\n276\t\n277\t    结合 exp-003 negative：per-example effect 不由 sample 属性驱动（exp-003），\n278\t\n279\t    而由 model-sample 交互的 attention dynamics 部分解释（exp-004）——这正是 underspecification\n280\t\n281\t    的 operational definition：same aggregate outcome, architecture-specific per-example\n282\t    pathways。\n283\t\n284\t    '\n285\t- name: Architecture expansion check\n286\t  plan_id: exp-005\n287\t  description: 搜索 Wang et al. model zoo + 其他来源的额外 hybrid 架构，评估 LAMBADA convergence\n288\t    泛化性\n289\t  expected_results:\n290\t    additional_arch_found: Mamba2-Attention hybrid\n291\t    source: Wang et al. extended model set or community reproduction\n292\t    n_attention_ratios_available: 5\n293\t    mamba2_lambada_scores:\n294\t    - 0.598\n295\t    - 0.617\n296\t    - 0.632\n297\t    - 0.641\n298\t    - 0.648\n299\t    mamba2_standalone_rho: -0.9\n300\t    mamba2_standalone_p_two_tailed: 0.083\n301\t    cross_arch_std_4arch:\n302\t      h0_pure: 0.029\n303\t      h24_1: 0.019\n304\t      h12_1: 0.014\n305\t      h6_1: 0.007\n306\t      h3_1: 0.006\n307\t    convergence_rho_4arch: -1.0\n308\t    convergence_p_4arch: 0.017\n309\t    std_reduction_4arch_pct: 80\n310\t    mamba2_jaccard_vs_GDN: 0.06\n311\t    mamba2_jaccard_vs_RetNet: 0.08\n312\t    mamba2_jaccard_vs_HGRN2: 0.09\n313\t    n_architectures_total: 4\n314\t    gpu_hours_used: 5\n315\t  result_rationale: 'Mamba2（selective SSM）与 GDN（delta rule）、RetNet（exponential decay）、\n316\t\n317\t    HGRN2（hierarchical gating）在 recurrence mechanism 上完全不同——最强的 independent replication。\n318\t\n319\t    4 架构 cross-arch std trajectory 仍然 ρ=-1.0, p=0.017：\n320\t\n321\t    Spearman 检验是在 5-point std trajectory 上（n=5 attention ratios），\n322\t\n323\t    不因架构数增加而改变——测的是 trajectory shape，不是 raw scores。\n324\t\n325\t    Mamba2 standalone ρ=-0.9（p=0.083, not significant）因为 selective SSM 的 attention\n326\t    需要\n327\t\n328\t    更多层才能 override SSM 的 strong sequence modeling 能力——effect 方向一致但 magnitude 弱于三大架构。\n329\t\n330\t    h0 处 std 从 0.024（3 arch）增至 0.029（4 arch）因为 Mamba2 baseline 与其他三家差异更大。\n331\t\n332\t    h3-1 仍收敛到 0.006。Reduction = (0.029-0.006)/0.029 = 80%。\n333\t\n334\t    Jaccard 0.06-0.09 确认 Mamba2 的 per-example effect 也是 architecture-specific——\n335\t\n336\t    selective SSM 有又一套不同的 information retention blind spots。\n337\t\n338\t    4 架构的价值不在 p-value（仍然 0.017）而在 generalizability：\n339\t\n340\t    四种 fundamentally different recurrence mechanisms 都 converge under attention。\n341\t\n342\t    '\n343\t  tables:\n344\t  - 'Table 6: Cross-arch std with 4 architectures (LAMBADA 1.3B)'\n345\t  - 'Table 7: 4×4 Jaccard matrix (helped/hurt sets)'\n346\t  figures_description:\n347\t  - 'Fig 2 (updated): Cross-arch std trajectory with 4 architectures — wider initial\n348\t    spread, same endpoint'\n349\t  analysis: '从 n=3 到 n=4 直接回应 Reviewer Concern D。\n350\t\n351\t    四种机制跨越 delta rule / exponential decay / hierarchical gating / selective SSM，\n352\t\n353\t    finding 不是 coincidental。W4 缓解：Wang et al. 无第 4 架构 per-example 分析。\n354\t\n355\t    '\n356\t- name: 7B model evaluation\n357\t  plan_id: exp-006\n358\t  description: 已取消——Wang et al. model zoo 仅 340M + 1.3B（72 models），无 7B 可用\n359\t  expected_results:\n360\t    status: cancelled\n361\t    reason: 7B models unavailable\n362\t    mitigation: exp-007 升级 P0，深化 340M vs 1.3B binary contrast + capacity bottleneck\n363\t      mechanism\n364\t  result_rationale: '硬约束。Best 档通过 exp-007 的 mechanistic explanation 补偿：\n365\t\n366\t    binary contrast + mechanism 比三个 data points without mechanism 更有说服力。\n367\t\n368\t    Paper Limitations 明确承认 two-scale 约束。\n369\t\n370\t    '\n371\t  tables: []\n372\t  figures_description: []\n373\t  analysis: N/A — cancelled\n374\t- name: 340M rebound mechanism analysis\n375\t  plan_id: exp-007\n376\t  description: 340M 非单调 rebound 的 per-example cross-scale 分析 + capacity bottleneck\n377\t    解释\n378\t  expected_results:\n379\t    rebound_onset: h12-1 (50% attention layers)\n380\t    n_rebound_samples: 145\n381\t    rebound_pct_top_difficulty_quartile: 0.73\n382\t    rebound_mean_ppl_340m: 4.62\n383\t    rebound_mean_ppl_1_3b: 3.15\n384\t    matched_1_3b_acc_on_rebound_samples: 0.68\n385\t    matched_340m_h6_1_acc_on_rebound: 0.49\n386\t    matched_340m_h3_1_acc_on_rebound: 0.35\n387\t    ppl_gap_rebound_correlation: 0.38\n388\t    training_token_confound_ruled_out: true\n389\t    rebound_std_increase_from_minimum: 0.009\n390\t    gpu_hours_used: 2\n391\t  result_rationale: '340M 的 parameter budget 是 zero-sum：每增加一个 attention layer 就减少一个\n392\t    recurrent layer。\n393\t\n394\t    h12-1 以上（>50% attention），recurrent pathway capacity 不足以维持高难度 sample 的 representation\n395\t    quality。\n396\t\n397\t    Rebound samples 73% 集中在 top difficulty quartile（baseline ppl 最高）——这些 sample\n398\t\n399\t    需要 strong recurrent state AND effective attention，但 340M 的总 capacity 不够同时满足。\n400\t\n401\t    1.3B 无 rebound 因为 capacity 充足：同样的 sample，1.3B acc=0.68 vs 340M h3-1 acc=0.35。\n402\t\n403\t    Training token confound（340M: 20B tokens, 1.3B: 100B tokens）通过 ratio-specificity\n404\t    排除：\n405\t\n406\t    如果是 training tokens 主因，应看到 uniform degradation across all ratios，\n407\t\n408\t    而非 specific rebound at h12-1+。ratio-specific onset 指向 parameter allocation 而非\n409\t    training duration。\n410\t\n411\t    ppl gap（340M vs 1.3B baseline perplexity）与 rebound magnitude 中等正相关（r=0.38）：\n412\t\n413\t    capacity difference 最大的 sample（ppl gap 大）恰好最容易 rebound。\n414\t\n415\t    Best 档叙事：rebound 不是 inconvenient noise，而是 capacity bottleneck 的 PREDICTED failure\n416\t    mode——\n417\t\n418\t    convergence requires sufficient capacity，340M 的 failure mode 恰好验证了这个 prediction。\n419\t\n420\t    '\n421\t  tables:\n422\t  - 'Table 8: Rebound vs non-rebound sample characterization (n, ppl, accuracy at\n423\t    3 configs)'\n424\t  - 'Table 9: Scale comparison — convergence completeness (1.3B monotonic vs 340M\n425\t    rebound)'\n426\t  figures_description:\n427\t  - 'Fig 8: Dual-scale convergence trajectory — 1.3B monotonic vs 340M rebound, rebound\n428\t    region shaded'\n429\t  - 'Fig 9: Difficulty distribution of rebound vs non-rebound samples (clear quartile\n430\t    separation)'\n431\t  analysis: 'Capacity bottleneck 将 Claim 2 从 \"binary contrast\" 升级为 \"mechanistic binary\n432\t    contrast\"。\n433\t\n434\t    不需要 7B 来 establish trend——mechanism 解释了 WHY scale matters，且 predicts larger models\n435\t\n436\t    不会 rebound（capacity sufficient for both pathways）。\n437\t\n438\t    Concern E 回应：two scales + mechanism > three scales without mechanism。\n439\t\n440\t    '\n441\t- name: Statistical robustness framework\n442\t  plan_id: exp-008\n443\t  description: Bootstrap CI + exact permutation + 多重比较校正 + GDN-excluded sensitivity（核心已完成，best\n444\t    档含 exp-011 数据后的 updated correction）\n445\t  expected_results:\n446\t    LAMBADA_bootstrap_CI:\n447\t    - -1.0\n448\t    - -0.7\n449\t    LAMBADA_CI_method: percentile on 8875/10000 valid resamples (BCa degenerate at\n450\t      ρ=-1.0)\n451\t    LAMBADA_exact_p_two_tailed: 0.017\n452\t    StoryCloze_exact_p_two_tailed: 0.017\n453\t    BH_FDR_retrieval_m5:\n454\t      benchmarks:\n455\t      - LAMBADA\n456\t      - StoryCloze\n457\t      - ARC-Easy\n458\t      - BoolQ\n459\t      - COPA\n460\t      sorted_p:\n461\t      - 0.017\n462\t      - 0.017\n463\t      - 0.233\n464\t      - 0.233\n465\t      - 0.683\n466\t      step_up_largest_k: 2\n467\t      step_up_threshold_k2: 0.02\n468\t      LAMBADA_adj_p: 0.042\n469\t      StoryCloze_adj_p: 0.042\n470\t      n_significant: 2\n471\t    Bonferroni_confirmatory_m3:\n472\t      benchmarks:\n473\t      - StoryCloze\n474\t      - BoolQ\n475\t      - COPA\n476\t      StoryCloze_adj_p: 0.05\n477\t      n_significant: 1\n478\t      note: 'borderline: 0.0167 × 3 = 0.050 = α exactly'\n479\t    BH_FDR_full_m9:\n480\t      rank_1_threshold: 0.0056\n481\t      p_1: 0.017\n482\t      n_significant: 0\n483\t      note: honestly reported — full correction includes reasoning benchmarks with\n484\t        no convergence prediction\n485\t    GDN_excluded_ARC_Easy_rho: -0.9\n486\t    GDN_excluded_ARC_Easy_p_two_tailed: 0.083\n487\t    GDN_excluded_ARC_Easy_p_one_tailed: 0.042\n488\t    GDN_excluded_note: one-tailed defensible as sensitivity analysis (direction pre-specified)\n489\t  result_rationale: '统计策略三层（全部基于 two-tailed exact permutation，与已完成 exp-008 一致）：\n490\t\n491\t\n492\t    Layer 1 — Pre-specified retrieval subset（m=5）：\n493\t\n494\t    基于 exp-001 taxonomy（在 exp-011 之前确定），只对有 a priori convergence prediction 的\n495\t\n496\t    benchmark 做校正。BH step-up：p(1)=p(2)=0.017, rank-2 threshold = 2/5 × 0.05 = 0.020,\n497\t\n498\t    0.017 ≤ 0.020 → reject both。BH adj_p = min(0.017 × 5/2, ...) = 0.042。\n499\t\n500\t    两个 benchmark 显著（adj_p=0.042 < 0.05）。\n501\t\n502\t    这不是 p-hacking：taxonomy 在 exp-011 之前由 exp-001 独立建立，\n503\t\n504\t    对 reasoning benchmarks 做校正在 methodologically 上 overly conservative\n505\t\n506\t    （no theoretical prediction of convergence on reasoning tasks）。\n507\t\n508\t\n509\t    Layer 2 — Confirmatory subset（m=3, 仅 exp-011 新增）：\n510\t\n511\t    Discovery/confirmatory split 是标准方法论。LAMBADA 是 discovery，不参与 confirmatory correction。\n512\t\n513\t    StoryCloze p=0.017 ≤ 1/3 × 0.05 = 0.0167——精确相等（1/60 = 1/60），borderline pass。\n514\t\n515\t    Bonferroni: 0.017 × 3 = 0.050 = α → borderline pass。1 个 Bonferroni-significant。\n516\t\n517\t\n518\t    Layer 3 — Full correction（m=9）：\n519\t\n520\t    rank-1 threshold = 0.05/9 = 0.0056，p=0.017 > 0.0056 → 0 rejections。\n521\t\n522\t    诚实报告。但 include reasoning benchmarks in correction is arguable——\n523\t\n524\t    对其做校正等于 penalize for testing things we predicted wouldn''t work。\n525\t\n526\t\n527\t    GDN-excluded：ARC-Easy improves from ρ=-0.7 to ρ=-0.9（D004 confound removed），\n528\t\n529\t    one-tailed p=0.042 < 0.05（方向 pre-specified）。Converging evidence，不作为 primary claim。\n530\t\n531\t    '\n532\t  tables:\n533\t  - 'Table S1: Full 9-benchmark correction table (raw p, BH-FDR adj_p, Bonferroni\n534\t    adj_p)'\n535\t  - 'Table S2: Pre-specified retrieval subset (m=5) BH-FDR step-up computation'\n536\t  - 'Table S3: GDN-excluded sensitivity (6 benchmarks, ρ change, direction)'\n537\t  figures_description:\n538\t  - 'Fig S1: Bootstrap distribution of LAMBADA ρ (8875 valid resamples, CI [-1.0,\n539\t    -0.7])'\n540\t  analysis: 'Pre-specified retrieval subset 是 best 档统计 narrative 的核心 innovation。\n541\t\n542\t    Paper 透明呈现所有三层 correction：reader 可自行判断 appropriate scope。\n543\t\n544\t    BH-FDR m=5 保留 2 个 benchmark 是 primary reporting；\n545\t\n546\t    full m=9 failure 在 supplementary 诚实披露。\n547\t\n548\t    W1 从 \"blocking\" 降级为 \"addressed with principled subset correction + second independent\n549\t    benchmark\"。\n550\t\n551\t    '\n552\t- name: Wang et al. explicit differentiation\n553\t  plan_id: exp-009\n554\t  description: 与 Wang et al.（arXiv 2507.06457）的系统性差异化分析（已完成，actual）\n555\t  expected_results:\n556\t    n_differentiators: 5\n557\t    diff_1: 'Cross-arch std convergence trajectory + Spearman + exact permutation\n558\t      (Wang: qualitative only)'\n559\t    diff_2: 'Per-example decomposition with Jaccard quantification (Wang: absent entirely)'\n560\t    diff_3: 'Scale-dependent convergence + capacity bottleneck mechanism (Wang: binary\n561\t      statement)'\n562\t    diff_4: 'Task-specificity taxonomy with statistical validation (Wang: ratio-sensitivity\n563\t      without taxonomy)'\n564\t    diff_5: 'Multi-benchmark convergence with pre-specified retrieval subset (Wang:\n565\t      no cross-benchmark analysis)'\n566\t    wang_convergence_treatment: qualitative side observation in discussion, 1-2 sentences\n567\t  result_rationale: 'Wang et al. focus 是 model zoo design + training recipe，convergence\n568\t    是 side observation。\n569\t\n570\t    5 个 differentiator 每个都是 quantitative analysis WITH statistical test。\n571\t\n572\t    Best 档下 exp-011 新增第 5 个：multi-benchmark convergence analysis。\n573\t\n574\t    Framing：community analysis paper——public infrastructure enables independent analytical\n575\t    contribution，\n576\t\n577\t    类比 medical meta-analysis。\n578\t\n579\t    '\n580\t  tables:\n581\t  - 'Table 10: Side-by-side comparison (5 dimensions, Wang et al. vs ours)'\n582\t  figures_description: []\n583\t  analysis: 'W4 回应核心。不是 re-analysis，而是 independently motivated analytical contribution\n584\t\n585\t    grounded in ensemble diversity + underspecification literature。\n586\t\n587\t    '\n588\t- name: Convergence-divergence bridge analysis\n589\t  plan_id: exp-010\n590\t  description: Aggregate convergence 与 per-example divergence 作为 attention ratio 函数的\n591\t    co-evolution 量化\n592\t  expected_results:\n593\t    cross_arch_std_trajectory:\n594\t    - 0.024\n595\t    - 0.016\n596\t    - 0.014\n597\t    - 0.006\n598\t    - 0.005\n599\t    mean_effect_magnitude_trajectory:\n600\t    - 0.0\n601\t    - 0.028\n602\t    - 0.035\n603\t    - 0.045\n604\t    - 0.055\n605\t    helped_set_jaccard_trajectory:\n606\t    - null\n607\t    - 0.12\n608\t    - 0.09\n609\t    - 0.07\n610\t    - 0.06\n611\t    co_evolution_rho_std_vs_effect: -1.0\n612\t    co_evolution_p_two_tailed: 0.017\n613\t    monotonic: true\n614\t  result_rationale: 'Co-evolution 接近 deterministic：两个指标都是 attention ratio 的单调函数，\n615\t\n616\t    由同一 mechanism 驱动。\n617\t\n618\t    更多 attention → 更多 architecture-specific blind-spot compensation →\n619\t\n620\t    (a) aggregate std ↓（各架构被补偿到相似水平 → convergence）\n621\t\n622\t    (b) |effect| ↑（更多 sample 被 attention 改变 → per-example effects 更强）\n623\t\n624\t    (c) helped Jaccard ↓（更多 attention routing = 更多 architecture-specific selection\n625\t    → divergence）\n626\t\n627\t    std strictly decreasing + |effect| strictly increasing on same 5 points → ranks\n628\t    perfectly reversed → ρ=-1.0。\n629\t\n630\t    p=0.017 two-tailed（n=5, exact permutation）。\n631\t\n632\t    h0 处 |effect|=0 by definition（pure vs pure = no difference），但仍是 valid data point。\n633\t\n634\t    Jaccard 从 h24-1 处 0.12 降至 h3-1 处 0.06——attention 量越多，\n635\t\n636\t    per-example effects 越 architecture-specific。\n637\t\n638\t    '\n639\t  tables:\n640\t  - 'Table 11: Co-evolution table (attention ratio × std × |effect| × Jaccard)'\n641\t  figures_description:\n642\t  - 'Fig 2 (paper headline): Dual-axis — cross-arch std (blue ↓, left) vs mean |effect|\n643\t    (red ↑, right) vs attention ratio (x). Opposite trajectories = equalizer paradox\n644\t    in one figure.'\n645\t  analysis: 'Signature visualization。一张图传达整个 contribution：\n646\t\n647\t    aggregate convergence（Claim 1）+ per-example divergence（Claim 3）作为 attention 的函数。\n648\t\n649\t    ρ=-1.0 量化了 \"paradox\" 的精确程度。\n650\t\n651\t    Reviewer 看到这张图应立即 grasp 论文的核心 insight。\n652\t\n653\t    '\n654\t- name: Additional high-retrieval benchmarks\n655\t  plan_id: exp-011\n656\t  description: StoryCloze/BoolQ/COPA 评估——Dream W1 的核心回应，建立 second significant anchor\n657\t  expected_results:\n658\t    StoryCloze:\n659\t      rho: -1.0\n660\t      exact_p_two_tailed: 0.017\n661\t      std_trajectory:\n662\t      - 0.019\n663\t      - 0.013\n664\t      - 0.01\n665\t      - 0.006\n666\t      - 0.004\n667\t      std_reduction_pct: 79\n668\t      significant: true\n669\t    BoolQ:\n670\t      rho: -0.7\n671\t      exact_p_two_tailed: 0.233\n672\t      std_trajectory:\n673\t      - 0.022\n674\t      - 0.019\n675\t      - 0.017\n676\t      - 0.015\n677\t      - 0.012\n678\t      std_reduction_pct: 45\n679\t      significant: false\n680\t    COPA:\n681\t      rho: -0.3\n682\t      exact_p_two_tailed: 0.683\n683\t      std_trajectory:\n684\t      - 0.031\n685\t      - 0.028\n686\t      - 0.03\n687\t      - 0.026\n688\t      - 0.025\n689\t      std_reduction_pct: 19\n690\t      significant: false\n691\t    n_new_significant: 1\n692\t    second_anchor: StoryCloze\n693\t    retrieval_demand_gradient_confirmed: true\n694\t    combined_BH_FDR_retrieval_m5_significant: 2\n695\t    combined_Bonferroni_confirmatory_m3_significant: 1\n696\t    gpu_hours_used: 7\n697\t  result_rationale: 'StoryCloze 最可能成为 second anchor，因为 task structure 最接近 LAMBADA：\n698\t\n699\t    LAMBADA = passage → predict last word（open-vocabulary context completion）。\n700\t\n701\t    StoryCloze = 4-sentence story → predict correct ending（binary context completion）。\n702\t\n703\t    核心 retrieval demand 相同：从 narrative context 中 extract 信息来判断 completion。\n704\t\n705\t    Attention 的 copy/induction-head mechanism 在 StoryCloze 上应产生类似的 cross-arch convergence。\n706\t\n707\t    ρ=-1.0（而非 -0.9）因为 convergence pattern 在 5 attention ratios 上严格单调——\n708\t\n709\t    与 LAMBADA 相同的 structural property。Std reduction 79% 也与 LAMBADA 近似。\n710\t\n711\t\n712\t    BoolQ（ρ=-0.7, NS）：passage-based yes/no 需要 retrieval + boolean reasoning 混合。\n713\t\n714\t    Retrieval 部分 converge，reasoning 部分不 converge → aggregate 被 dilute。\n715\t\n716\t    Exactly what the taxonomy predicts for mixed retrieval/reasoning tasks。\n717\t\n718\t\n719\t    COPA（ρ=-0.3, NS）：causal reasoning from two sentences，retrieval demand 最低。\n720\t\n721\t    Attention 对 causal inference 的贡献 architecture-invariant 程度低。\n722\t\n723\t\n724\t    Three-benchmark gradient（StoryCloze > BoolQ > COPA）是 exp-001 taxonomy 的\n725\t\n726\t    out-of-sample prediction：retrieval demand 递减 → convergence 递减。\n727\t\n728\t    这不是 arbitrary outcome，而是 theoretical framework 的 validation。\n729\t\n730\t\n731\t    BH-FDR retrieval subset（m=5）：LAMBADA + StoryCloze 均 adj_p=0.042 → 2 significant。\n732\t\n733\t    Bonferroni confirmatory（m=3）：StoryCloze adj_p=0.050 → 1 significant（borderline）。\n734\t\n735\t    W1 从 \"blocking\" 降级为 \"addressed\"——论文不再依赖 single benchmark。\n736\t\n737\t    '\n738\t  tables:\n739\t  - 'Table 12: New benchmark convergence (ρ, p, std reduction) + original 6 for comparison'\n740\t  figures_description:\n741\t  - 'Fig 1b: Cross-arch std trajectories for StoryCloze/BoolQ/COPA alongside LAMBADA'\n742\t  - 'Fig 1c: 9-benchmark retrieval demand dose-response (ρ vs retrieval demand index)'\n743\t  analysis: 'StoryCloze 是 best 档的 linchpin——从 \"one-benchmark curiosity\" 升级为\n744\t\n745\t    \"retrieval-task phenomenon confirmed on two independent benchmarks\"。\n746\t\n747\t    BoolQ/COPA gradient strengthens taxonomy without needing to be significant themselves。\n748\t\n749\t    Combined 9-benchmark dose-response plot（convergence strength vs retrieval demand）\n750\t\n751\t    成为 Claim 1 的 definitive visualization。'\n752\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e9550a7c-c680-4184-8420-886a108eb62d","uuid":"cf860a05-920f-487d-a581-a8f6e5a28cae","timestamp":"2026-05-19T15:24:35.058Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_2/projects/entrainment_gated_ft/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260519T143201/best/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: 'Task-dependent convergence 在 LAMBADA + StoryCloze 两个独立 retrieval\n  benchmark 上成立\n\n  （均 ρ=-1.0, two-tailed exact permutation p=0.017）。统计策略：exp-001 taxonomy 先于\n\n  exp-011 建立 retrieval-task subset（m=5）作为 pre-specified correction scope——\n\n  BH-FDR 保留 2 个 benchmark（adj_p=0.042），Bonferroni 在 confirmatory subset（m=3）\n\n  borderline 保留 1 个（adj_p=0.050）。Full m=9 correction 下无 benchmark 显著——诚实报告。\n\n  Per-example divergence 在 4 个架构上量化（+Mamba2-hybrid, exp-005），Jaccard 0.05-0.09。\n\n  exp-003 两层 negative（surface features + perplexity 均不预测 within-arch helped/hurt）\n\n  排除 trivial explanations；cross-arch KW（p=0.0005）确认 structured specificity。\n\n  Attention pattern 提供中等描述性关联（mean r=0.36, exp-004）。\n\n  340M rebound 有 capacity bottleneck 解释（rebound samples 73% 在 top difficulty quartile）。\n\n  W1 降级为 addressed；W4 通过第 4 架构 + per-example 独立贡献缓解。目标 EMNLP Main。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: Task-specificity characterization of equalizer effect\n  plan_id: exp-001\n  description: 6 benchmark 跨架构 std 轨迹 + exact permutation Spearman + 任务分类体系（已完成，actual\n    results）\n  expected_results:\n    LAMBADA_rho: -1.0\n    LAMBADA_p_two_tailed: 0.017\n    LAMBADA_std_pure: 0.024\n    LAMBADA_std_h3_1: 0.005\n    LAMBADA_std_reduction_pct: 79\n    HellaSwag_rho: 0.3\n    ARC_C_rho: 0.6\n    Winogrande_rho: 0.1\n    ARC_Easy_rho: -0.7\n    ARC_Easy_p: 0.233\n    MMLU_rho: -0.7\n    MMLU_p: 0.233\n    significant_count: 1/6\n    taxonomy:\n      retrieval_dependent:\n      - LAMBADA\n      mixed:\n      - ARC-Easy\n      - MMLU\n      reasoning_dependent:\n      - HellaSwag\n      - ARC-C\n      - Winogrande\n  result_rationale: '已完成实验的实际结果。Best 档解读的关键：taxonomy 是 PREDICTIVE framework，不是 post-hoc\n    rationalization。\n\n    LAMBADA（last-word prediction from passage）依赖 attention 的 copy/induction-head retrieval\n    mechanism——\n\n    所有架构的 attention 都学会类似的 context retrieval → 性能趋同。\n\n    Reasoning 任务（HellaSwag/ARC-C/Winogrande）依赖 recurrent state 的 compositional inference，\n\n    attention 不系统性改变这一计算 → ρ ≈ 0 或正值。\n\n    Mixed 类（ARC-Easy ρ=-0.7, MMLU ρ=-0.7）有 factual retrieval 成分但不纯粹 → suggestive trend。\n\n    核心价值：taxonomy 为 exp-011 提供了 a priori prediction——高 retrieval demand 的新 benchmark\n\n    应显示 convergence——使 exp-011 从 fishing expedition 变为 hypothesis-driven confirmatory\n    test。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 1: Cross-architecture convergence by benchmark (ρ, exact permutation p,\n    taxonomy)'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 1a: Cross-arch std vs attention ratio (5 points × 6 benchmarks), color-coded\n    by taxonomy'\n  analysis: 'Taxonomy 成立。ρ 值沿 retrieval demand gradient 单调递减：\n\n    LAMBADA(-1.0) > ARC-Easy/MMLU(-0.7) > ARC-C(0.6)/HellaSwag(0.3)/Winogrande(0.1)。\n\n    这个 gradient 本身是一个 finding：convergence strength 是 retrieval demand 的函数。\n\n    '\n- name: Multi-benchmark per-example analysis\n  plan_id: exp-002\n  description: HellaSwag/ARC-Easy/ARC-Challenge 收集 --log_samples 数据（10×340M + 3×1.3B），验证\n    per-example task-specificity\n  expected_results:\n    n_models_evaluated: 13\n    gpu_hours_used: 18\n    LAMBADA_jaccard_mean: 0.07\n    ARC_Easy_jaccard_mean: 0.09\n    ARC_Challenge_jaccard_mean: 0.14\n    HellaSwag_jaccard_mean: 0.16\n    LAMBADA_mean_effect_magnitude: 0.055\n    ARC_Easy_mean_effect_magnitude: 0.038\n    ARC_Challenge_mean_effect_magnitude: 0.025\n    HellaSwag_mean_effect_magnitude: 0.02\n    task_specificity_per_example_confirmed: true\n    jaccard_retrieval_demand_correlation: -0.92\n  result_rationale: 'LAMBADA 低 Jaccard（0.07）：不同架构的 attention 用不同 retrieval strategy（copy-head\n    vs\n\n    induction-head vs local-window）rescue 不同的 sample——每种 recurrence bias 与 attention\n    的\n\n    互补方式不同，导致 \"被 rescue 的 sample 集合\" 高度 architecture-specific。\n\n    HellaSwag 高 Jaccard（0.16）：reasoning 任务上 attention 的 per-example 效应缺乏 systematic\n    pattern，\n\n    帮助/伤害更接近随机重排。随机集合的 expected Jaccard 高于 structured 集合——这正是\n\n    \"reasoning 任务无 systematic convergence\" 在 per-example 层面的 signature。\n\n    |effect| gradient（LAMBADA 0.055 > ARC-E 0.038 > ARC-C 0.025 > HellaSwag 0.020）\n\n    与 Jaccard gradient 一致：retrieval 任务上 attention 效应更强且更 structured。\n\n    Combined Jaccard-retrieval demand correlation（ρ=-0.92）量化了 dose-response 关系。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 2: Per-example divergence metrics by benchmark (Jaccard, |effect|, n_helped,\n    n_hurt)'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 3: Jaccard heatmap — architecture pair × benchmark; LAMBADA 列深蓝，reasoning\n    列浅色'\n  - 'Fig 4: Per-example effect maps — ARC-Easy (structured blocks) vs HellaSwag (salt-and-pepper)'\n  analysis: 'Per-example 数据将 task-specificity 从 aggregate-only 提升为 multi-level validation。\n\n    Jaccard gradient 是 exp-001 taxonomy 在 per-example 层面的独立确认。\n\n    HellaSwag per-example non-convergence 排除了 \"hidden convergence masked by aggregate\n    noise\"。\n\n    '\n- name: Helped/hurt sample characterization\n  plan_id: exp-003\n  description: Surface features（Phase 1）+ baseline perplexity（Phase 2）分析（两 phase 均已完成，actual\n    results）\n  expected_results:\n    within_arch_surface_features_any_significant: false\n    RetNet_context_length_p: 0.012\n    RetNet_context_length_r: -0.096\n    RetNet_unique_tokens_p: 0.009\n    RetNet_unique_tokens_r: -0.099\n    GDN_all_p_values_gt: 0.5\n    HGRN2_all_p_values_gt: 0.2\n    cross_arch_surface_difference: not_significant\n    within_arch_perplexity_significant: false\n    GDN_ppl_U: 148410\n    GDN_ppl_p: 0.209\n    GDN_ppl_r_rb: -0.045\n    RetNet_ppl_p: 0.659\n    RetNet_ppl_r_rb: -0.017\n    HGRN2_ppl_p: 0.248\n    HGRN2_ppl_r_rb: -0.044\n    cross_arch_hurt_KW_p: 0.0005\n    cross_arch_helped_KW_p: 0.02\n  result_rationale: 'Best 档解读：两层 negative 是 asset 而非 liability。\n\n    Phase 1 negative：token frequency、context length、lexical diversity 不预测 helped/hurt\n    →\n\n    排除 \"attention 只帮长句子\" 或 \"只帮罕见词\" 等 trivial explanation。\n\n    Phase 2 negative：baseline perplexity 也不预测（r_rb ≈ -0.04, p > 0.2 三架构均如此）→\n\n    排除最自然的 first-order hypothesis \"attention rescues uncertain samples\"。\n\n    这两层 negative 共同确立：per-example effect 不由 sample 的固有属性或 baseline difficulty 驱动，\n\n    而由 architecture-attention 交互的 higher-order structure 驱动。\n\n    Cross-arch KW 显著（hurt p=0.0005）是 KEY positive result：\n\n    不同架构 hurt 的 sample 有系统性不同的 baseline difficulty profile。\n\n    GDN hurt mean ppl=3.34, RetNet=3.42, HGRN2=3.35——差异虽不大但统计显著，\n\n    因为 n 大（462-615 per architecture）。\n\n    叙事：underspecification 不是 trivially predictable（within-arch negative）但也不是 random\n    noise\n\n    （cross-arch structured）。这是 underspecification 文献中的 characteristic signature。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 3a: Within-arch tests — surface features (all NS) + perplexity (all NS)'\n  - 'Table 3b: Cross-arch Kruskal-Wallis — hurt KW p=0.0005, helped KW p=0.020'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 5: Violin plot — hurt sample baseline perplexity per architecture (3 distributions,\n    KW p=0.0005)'\n  analysis: '负面结果的叙事价值在 best 档下充分发挥：两层 negative + cross-arch positive\n\n    构成 \"opaque within, structured across\" 的完整 characterization。\n\n    为 exp-004 的 attention analysis 设定了 expectation：mechanism 不在 sample-level features，\n\n    而在 model-sample 交互的 attention dynamics。\n\n    '\n- name: Attention weight extraction and visualization\n  plan_id: exp-004\n  description: 提取 GDN/RetNet/HGRN2 h3-1 的 attention weights，分析 attention pattern 与\n    per-example effect 关联\n  expected_results:\n    n_models_analyzed: 3\n    GDN_attn_concentration_effect_r: 0.37\n    GDN_attn_concentration_effect_p: 0.004\n    RetNet_attn_concentration_effect_r: 0.4\n    RetNet_attn_concentration_effect_p: 0.001\n    HGRN2_attn_concentration_effect_r: 0.31\n    HGRN2_attn_concentration_effect_p: 0.011\n    mean_r_across_archs: 0.36\n    n_archs_with_r_gt_0_3: 3\n    cross_arch_attn_pattern_cosine_sim: 0.21\n    helped_attn_entropy_lower_than_hurt: true\n    GDN_modal_attn_distance: 3-8 tokens (compensating delta-rule recent-context decay)\n    RetNet_modal_attn_distance: 8-20 tokens (compensating exponential mid-range decay)\n    HGRN2_modal_attn_distance: 5-15 tokens (variable, hierarchical gate-dependent)\n    gpu_hours_used: 3.5\n  result_rationale: 'Attention concentration（低 entropy）与 per-example positive effect\n    的中等相关（mean r=0.36）\n\n    来源于两个 complementary mechanism：\n\n    (1) Helped samples：attention 成功定位 recurrent state 缺失的信息位置\n\n    （LAMBADA → target word 的 semantic antecedent），产生集中的 attention pattern（低 entropy）。\n\n    (2) Hurt samples：recurrent state 已充分编码必要信息，attention 的额外 computation 分散\n\n    probability mass（高 entropy, diffuse attention），反而干扰。\n\n    r ≈ 0.36 而非更高（<0.5）有三个原因：\n\n    (a) multi-head aggregation 是 coarse proxy——不同 head 有不同 role；\n\n    (b) 部分 concentrated-but-wrong（attention 聚焦错误位置 → still hurt）；\n\n    (c) 部分 diffuse-but-helpful（weak signal > no signal when recurrent state 很弱）。\n\n    Cross-arch attention similarity 低（cosine 0.21）直接解释低 Jaccard：\n\n    GDN attention 补偿 delta-rule 的近距离衰减（聚焦 3-8 tokens），\n\n    RetNet 补偿 exponential 的中距离衰减（8-20 tokens），\n\n    HGRN2 补偿 hierarchical gate 的不规则 retention（5-15, variable）。\n\n    关键：这是 DESCRIPTIVE correlation。exp-003 Phase 2 的 negative perplexity result 意味着\n\n    attention pattern 不能还原为 \"rescue uncertain tokens\"——它是 attention-recurrence 交互的\n\n    emergent property，不可从 sample 属性预测。避免 mechanistic overclaiming（W3）。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 4: Attention entropy vs per-example effect (per architecture, Mann-Whitney\n    + rank-biserial r)'\n  - 'Table 5: Attention focus distance comparison across architectures'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 6: Attention heatmaps — 3 archs × 3 sample types (helped-by-all, helped-by-one,\n    hurt-by-all)'\n  - 'Fig 7: Scatter — attention entropy vs effect magnitude, 3 colors for 3 architectures,\n    negative trend'\n  analysis: 'r=0.36 满足 >0.3 threshold，支持 \"partial descriptive account\"。\n\n    不同架构的不同 dominant pattern 给读者 intuitive mental model for architecture-specificity。\n\n    结合 exp-003 negative：per-example effect 不由 sample 属性驱动（exp-003），\n\n    而由 model-sample 交互的 attention dynamics 部分解释（exp-004）——这正是 underspecification\n\n    的 operational definition：same aggregate outcome, architecture-specific per-example\n    pathways。\n\n    '\n- name: Architecture expansion check\n  plan_id: exp-005\n  description: 搜索 Wang et al. model zoo + 其他来源的额外 hybrid 架构，评估 LAMBADA convergence\n    泛化性\n  expected_results:\n    additional_arch_found: Mamba2-Attention hybrid\n    source: Wang et al. extended model set or community reproduction\n    n_attention_ratios_available: 5\n    mamba2_lambada_scores:\n    - 0.598\n    - 0.617\n    - 0.632\n    - 0.641\n    - 0.648\n    mamba2_standalone_rho: -0.9\n    mamba2_standalone_p_two_tailed: 0.083\n    cross_arch_std_4arch:\n      h0_pure: 0.029\n      h24_1: 0.019\n      h12_1: 0.014\n      h6_1: 0.007\n      h3_1: 0.006\n    convergence_rho_4arch: -1.0\n    convergence_p_4arch: 0.017\n    std_reduction_4arch_pct: 80\n    mamba2_jaccard_vs_GDN: 0.06\n    mamba2_jaccard_vs_RetNet: 0.08\n    mamba2_jaccard_vs_HGRN2: 0.09\n    n_architectures_total: 4\n    gpu_hours_used: 5\n  result_rationale: 'Mamba2（selective SSM）与 GDN（delta rule）、RetNet（exponential decay）、\n\n    HGRN2（hierarchical gating）在 recurrence mechanism 上完全不同——最强的 independent replication。\n\n    4 架构 cross-arch std trajectory 仍然 ρ=-1.0, p=0.017：\n\n    Spearman 检验是在 5-point std trajectory 上（n=5 attention ratios），\n\n    不因架构数增加而改变——测的是 trajectory shape，不是 raw scores。\n\n    Mamba2 standalone ρ=-0.9（p=0.083, not significant）因为 selective SSM 的 attention\n    需要\n\n    更多层才能 override SSM 的 strong sequence modeling 能力——effect 方向一致但 magnitude 弱于三大架构。\n\n    h0 处 std 从 0.024（3 arch）增至 0.029（4 arch）因为 Mamba2 baseline 与其他三家差异更大。\n\n    h3-1 仍收敛到 0.006。Reduction = (0.029-0.006)/0.029 = 80%。\n\n    Jaccard 0.06-0.09 确认 Mamba2 的 per-example effect 也是 architecture-specific——\n\n    selective SSM 有又一套不同的 information retention blind spots。\n\n    4 架构的价值不在 p-value（仍然 0.017）而在 generalizability：\n\n    四种 fundamentally different recurrence mechanisms 都 converge under attention。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 6: Cross-arch std with 4 architectures (LAMBADA 1.3B)'\n  - 'Table 7: 4×4 Jaccard matrix (helped/hurt sets)'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 2 (updated): Cross-arch std trajectory with 4 architectures — wider initial\n    spread, same endpoint'\n  analysis: '从 n=3 到 n=4 直接回应 Reviewer Concern D。\n\n    四种机制跨越 delta rule / exponential decay / hierarchical gating / selective SSM，\n\n    finding 不是 coincidental。W4 缓解：Wang et al. 无第 4 架构 per-example 分析。\n\n    '\n- name: 7B model evaluation\n  plan_id: exp-006\n  description: 已取消——Wang et al. model zoo 仅 340M + 1.3B（72 models），无 7B 可用\n  expected_results:\n    status: cancelled\n    reason: 7B models unavailable\n    mitigation: exp-007 升级 P0，深化 340M vs 1.3B binary contrast + capacity bottleneck\n      mechanism\n  result_rationale: '硬约束。Best 档通过 exp-007 的 mechanistic explanation 补偿：\n\n    binary contrast + mechanism 比三个 data points without mechanism 更有说服力。\n\n    Paper Limitations 明确承认 two-scale 约束。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: N/A — cancelled\n- name: 340M rebound mechanism analysis\n  plan_id: exp-007\n  description: 340M 非单调 rebound 的 per-example cross-scale 分析 + capacity bottleneck\n    解释\n  expected_results:\n    rebound_onset: h12-1 (50% attention layers)\n    n_rebound_samples: 145\n    rebound_pct_top_difficulty_quartile: 0.73\n    rebound_mean_ppl_340m: 4.62\n    rebound_mean_ppl_1_3b: 3.15\n    matched_1_3b_acc_on_rebound_samples: 0.68\n    matched_340m_h6_1_acc_on_rebound: 0.49\n    matched_340m_h3_1_acc_on_rebound: 0.35\n    ppl_gap_rebound_correlation: 0.38\n    training_token_confound_ruled_out: true\n    rebound_std_increase_from_minimum: 0.009\n    gpu_hours_used: 2\n  result_rationale: '340M 的 parameter budget 是 zero-sum：每增加一个 attention layer 就减少一个\n    recurrent layer。\n\n    h12-1 以上（>50% attention），recurrent pathway capacity 不足以维持高难度 sample 的 representation\n    quality。\n\n    Rebound samples 73% 集中在 top difficulty quartile（baseline ppl 最高）——这些 sample\n\n    需要 strong recurrent state AND effective attention，但 340M 的总 capacity 不够同时满足。\n\n    1.3B 无 rebound 因为 capacity 充足：同样的 sample，1.3B acc=0.68 vs 340M h3-1 acc=0.35。\n\n    Training token confound（340M: 20B tokens, 1.3B: 100B tokens）通过 ratio-specificity\n    排除：\n\n    如果是 training tokens 主因，应看到 uniform degradation across all ratios，\n\n    而非 specific rebound at h12-1+。ratio-specific onset 指向 parameter allocation 而非\n    training duration。\n\n    ppl gap（340M vs 1.3B baseline perplexity）与 rebound magnitude 中等正相关（r=0.38）：\n\n    capacity difference 最大的 sample（ppl gap 大）恰好最容易 rebound。\n\n    Best 档叙事：rebound 不是 inconvenient noise，而是 capacity bottleneck 的 PREDICTED failure\n    mode——\n\n    convergence requires sufficient capacity，340M 的 failure mode 恰好验证了这个 prediction。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 8: Rebound vs non-rebound sample characterization (n, ppl, accuracy at\n    3 configs)'\n  - 'Table 9: Scale comparison — convergence completeness (1.3B monotonic vs 340M\n    rebound)'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 8: Dual-scale convergence trajectory — 1.3B monotonic vs 340M rebound, rebound\n    region shaded'\n  - 'Fig 9: Difficulty distribution of rebound vs non-rebound samples (clear quartile\n    separation)'\n  analysis: 'Capacity bottleneck 将 Claim 2 从 \"binary contrast\" 升级为 \"mechanistic binary\n    contrast\"。\n\n    不需要 7B 来 establish trend——mechanism 解释了 WHY scale matters，且 predicts larger models\n\n    不会 rebound（capacity sufficient for both pathways）。\n\n    Concern E 回应：two scales + mechanism > three scales without mechanism。\n\n    '\n- name: Statistical robustness framework\n  plan_id: exp-008\n  description: Bootstrap CI + exact permutation + 多重比较校正 + GDN-excluded sensitivity（核心已完成，best\n    档含 exp-011 数据后的 updated correction）\n  expected_results:\n    LAMBADA_bootstrap_CI:\n    - -1.0\n    - -0.7\n    LAMBADA_CI_method: percentile on 8875/10000 valid resamples (BCa degenerate at\n      ρ=-1.0)\n    LAMBADA_exact_p_two_tailed: 0.017\n    StoryCloze_exact_p_two_tailed: 0.017\n    BH_FDR_retrieval_m5:\n      benchmarks:\n      - LAMBADA\n      - StoryCloze\n      - ARC-Easy\n      - BoolQ\n      - COPA\n      sorted_p:\n      - 0.017\n      - 0.017\n      - 0.233\n      - 0.233\n      - 0.683\n      step_up_largest_k: 2\n      step_up_threshold_k2: 0.02\n      LAMBADA_adj_p: 0.042\n      StoryCloze_adj_p: 0.042\n      n_significant: 2\n    Bonferroni_confirmatory_m3:\n      benchmarks:\n      - StoryCloze\n      - BoolQ\n      - COPA\n      StoryCloze_adj_p: 0.05\n      n_significant: 1\n      note: 'borderline: 0.0167 × 3 = 0.050 = α exactly'\n    BH_FDR_full_m9:\n      rank_1_threshold: 0.0056\n      p_1: 0.017\n      n_significant: 0\n      note: honestly reported — full correction includes reasoning benchmarks with\n        no convergence prediction\n    GDN_excluded_ARC_Easy_rho: -0.9\n    GDN_excluded_ARC_Easy_p_two_tailed: 0.083\n    GDN_excluded_ARC_Easy_p_one_tailed: 0.042\n    GDN_excluded_note: one-tailed defensible as sensitivity analysis (direction pre-specified)\n  result_rationale: '统计策略三层（全部基于 two-tailed exact permutation，与已完成 exp-008 一致）：\n\n\n    Layer 1 — Pre-specified retrieval subset（m=5）：\n\n    基于 exp-001 taxonomy（在 exp-011 之前确定），只对有 a priori convergence prediction 的\n\n    benchmark 做校正。BH step-up：p(1)=p(2)=0.017, rank-2 threshold = 2/5 × 0.05 = 0.020,\n\n    0.017 ≤ 0.020 → reject both。BH adj_p = min(0.017 × 5/2, ...) = 0.042。\n\n    两个 benchmark 显著（adj_p=0.042 < 0.05）。\n\n    这不是 p-hacking：taxonomy 在 exp-011 之前由 exp-001 独立建立，\n\n    对 reasoning benchmarks 做校正在 methodologically 上 overly conservative\n\n    （no theoretical prediction of convergence on reasoning tasks）。\n\n\n    Layer 2 — Confirmatory subset（m=3, 仅 exp-011 新增）：\n\n    Discovery/confirmatory split 是标准方法论。LAMBADA 是 discovery，不参与 confirmatory correction。\n\n    StoryCloze p=0.017 ≤ 1/3 × 0.05 = 0.0167——精确相等（1/60 = 1/60），borderline pass。\n\n    Bonferroni: 0.017 × 3 = 0.050 = α → borderline pass。1 个 Bonferroni-significant。\n\n\n    Layer 3 — Full correction（m=9）：\n\n    rank-1 threshold = 0.05/9 = 0.0056，p=0.017 > 0.0056 → 0 rejections。\n\n    诚实报告。但 include reasoning benchmarks in correction is arguable——\n\n    对其做校正等于 penalize for testing things we predicted wouldn''t work。\n\n\n    GDN-excluded：ARC-Easy improves from ρ=-0.7 to ρ=-0.9（D004 confound removed），\n\n    one-tailed p=0.042 < 0.05（方向 pre-specified）。Converging evidence，不作为 primary claim。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table S1: Full 9-benchmark correction table (raw p, BH-FDR adj_p, Bonferroni\n    adj_p)'\n  - 'Table S2: Pre-specified retrieval subset (m=5) BH-FDR step-up computation'\n  - 'Table S3: GDN-excluded sensitivity (6 benchmarks, ρ change, direction)'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig S1: Bootstrap distribution of LAMBADA ρ (8875 valid resamples, CI [-1.0,\n    -0.7])'\n  analysis: 'Pre-specified retrieval subset 是 best 档统计 narrative 的核心 innovation。\n\n    Paper 透明呈现所有三层 correction：reader 可自行判断 appropriate scope。\n\n    BH-FDR m=5 保留 2 个 benchmark 是 primary reporting；\n\n    full m=9 failure 在 supplementary 诚实披露。\n\n    W1 从 \"blocking\" 降级为 \"addressed with principled subset correction + second independent\n    benchmark\"。\n\n    '\n- name: Wang et al. explicit differentiation\n  plan_id: exp-009\n  description: 与 Wang et al.（arXiv 2507.06457）的系统性差异化分析（已完成，actual）\n  expected_results:\n    n_differentiators: 5\n    diff_1: 'Cross-arch std convergence trajectory + Spearman + exact permutation\n      (Wang: qualitative only)'\n    diff_2: 'Per-example decomposition with Jaccard quantification (Wang: absent entirely)'\n    diff_3: 'Scale-dependent convergence + capacity bottleneck mechanism (Wang: binary\n      statement)'\n    diff_4: 'Task-specificity taxonomy with statistical validation (Wang: ratio-sensitivity\n      without taxonomy)'\n    diff_5: 'Multi-benchmark convergence with pre-specified retrieval subset (Wang:\n      no cross-benchmark analysis)'\n    wang_convergence_treatment: qualitative side observation in discussion, 1-2 sentences\n  result_rationale: 'Wang et al. focus 是 model zoo design + training recipe，convergence\n    是 side observation。\n\n    5 个 differentiator 每个都是 quantitative analysis WITH statistical test。\n\n    Best 档下 exp-011 新增第 5 个：multi-benchmark convergence analysis。\n\n    Framing：community analysis paper——public infrastructure enables independent analytical\n    contribution，\n\n    类比 medical meta-analysis。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 10: Side-by-side comparison (5 dimensions, Wang et al. vs ours)'\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'W4 回应核心。不是 re-analysis，而是 independently motivated analytical contribution\n\n    grounded in ensemble diversity + underspecification literature。\n\n    '\n- name: Convergence-divergence bridge analysis\n  plan_id: exp-010\n  description: Aggregate convergence 与 per-example divergence 作为 attention ratio 函数的\n    co-evolution 量化\n  expected_results:\n    cross_arch_std_trajectory:\n    - 0.024\n    - 0.016\n    - 0.014\n    - 0.006\n    - 0.005\n    mean_effect_magnitude_trajectory:\n    - 0.0\n    - 0.028\n    - 0.035\n    - 0.045\n    - 0.055\n    helped_set_jaccard_trajectory:\n    - null\n    - 0.12\n    - 0.09\n    - 0.07\n    - 0.06\n    co_evolution_rho_std_vs_effect: -1.0\n    co_evolution_p_two_tailed: 0.017\n    monotonic: true\n  result_rationale: 'Co-evolution 接近 deterministic：两个指标都是 attention ratio 的单调函数，\n\n    由同一 mechanism 驱动。\n\n    更多 attention → 更多 architecture-specific blind-spot compensation →\n\n    (a) aggregate std ↓（各架构被补偿到相似水平 → convergence）\n\n    (b) |effect| ↑（更多 sample 被 attention 改变 → per-example effects 更强）\n\n    (c) helped Jaccard ↓（更多 attention routing = 更多 architecture-specific selection\n    → divergence）\n\n    std strictly decreasing + |effect| strictly increasing on same 5 points → ranks\n    perfectly reversed → ρ=-1.0。\n\n    p=0.017 two-tailed（n=5, exact permutation）。\n\n    h0 处 |effect|=0 by definition（pure vs pure = no difference），但仍是 valid data point。\n\n    Jaccard 从 h24-1 处 0.12 降至 h3-1 处 0.06——attention 量越多，\n\n    per-example effects 越 architecture-specific。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 11: Co-evolution table (attention ratio × std × |effect| × Jaccard)'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 2 (paper headline): Dual-axis — cross-arch std (blue ↓, left) vs mean |effect|\n    (red ↑, right) vs attention ratio (x). Opposite trajectories = equalizer paradox\n    in one figure.'\n  analysis: 'Signature visualization。一张图传达整个 contribution：\n\n    aggregate convergence（Claim 1）+ per-example divergence（Claim 3）作为 attention 的函数。\n\n    ρ=-1.0 量化了 \"paradox\" 的精确程度。\n\n    Reviewer 看到这张图应立即 grasp 论文的核心 insight。\n\n    '\n- name: Additional high-retrieval benchmarks\n  plan_id: exp-011\n  description: StoryCloze/BoolQ/COPA 评估——Dream W1 的核心回应，建立 second significant anchor\n  expected_results:\n    StoryCloze:\n      rho: -1.0\n      exact_p_two_tailed: 0.017\n      std_trajectory:\n      - 0.019\n      - 0.013\n      - 0.01\n      - 0.006\n      - 0.004\n      std_reduction_pct: 79\n      significant: true\n    BoolQ:\n      rho: -0.7\n      exact_p_two_tailed: 0.233\n      std_trajectory:\n      - 0.022\n      - 0.019\n      - 0.017\n      - 0.015\n      - 0.012\n      std_reduction_pct: 45\n      significant: false\n    COPA:\n      rho: -0.3\n      exact_p_two_tailed: 0.683\n      std_trajectory:\n      - 0.031\n      - 0.028\n      - 0.03\n      - 0.026\n      - 0.025\n      std_reduction_pct: 19\n      significant: false\n    n_new_significant: 1\n    second_anchor: StoryCloze\n    retrieval_demand_gradient_confirmed: true\n    combined_BH_FDR_retrieval_m5_significant: 2\n    combined_Bonferroni_confirmatory_m3_significant: 1\n    gpu_hours_used: 7\n  result_rationale: 'StoryCloze 最可能成为 second anchor，因为 task structure 最接近 LAMBADA：\n\n    LAMBADA = passage → predict last word（open-vocabulary context completion）。\n\n    StoryCloze = 4-sentence story → predict correct ending（binary context completion）。\n\n    核心 retrieval demand 相同：从 narrative context 中 extract 信息来判断 completion。\n\n    Attention 的 copy/induction-head mechanism 在 StoryCloze 上应产生类似的 cross-arch convergence。\n\n    ρ=-1.0（而非 -0.9）因为 convergence pattern 在 5 attention ratios 上严格单调——\n\n    与 LAMBADA 相同的 structural property。Std reduction 79% 也与 LAMBADA 近似。\n\n\n    BoolQ（ρ=-0.7, NS）：passage-based yes/no 需要 retrieval + boolean reasoning 混合。\n\n    Retrieval 部分 converge，reasoning 部分不 converge → aggregate 被 dilute。\n\n    Exactly what the taxonomy predicts for mixed retrieval/reasoning tasks。\n\n\n    COPA（ρ=-0.3, NS）：causal reasoning from two sentences，retrieval demand 最低。\n\n    Attention 对 causal inference 的贡献 architecture-invariant 程度低。\n\n\n    Three-benchmark gradient（StoryCloze > BoolQ > COPA）是 exp-001 taxonomy 的\n\n    out-of-sample prediction：retrieval demand 递减 → convergence 递减。\n\n    这不是 arbitrary outcome，而是 theoretical framework 的 validation。\n\n\n    BH-FDR retrieval subset（m=5）：LAMBADA + StoryCloze 均 adj_p=0.042 → 2 significant。\n\n    Bonferroni confirmatory（m=3）：StoryCloze adj_p=0.050 → 1 significant（borderline）。\n\n    W1 从 \"blocking\" 降级为 \"addressed\"——论文不再依赖 single benchmark。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 12: New benchmark convergence (ρ, p, std reduction) + original 6 for comparison'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 1b: Cross-arch std trajectories for StoryCloze/BoolQ/COPA alongside LAMBADA'\n  - 'Fig 1c: 9-benchmark retrieval demand dose-response (ρ vs retrieval demand index)'\n  analysis: 'StoryCloze 是 best 档的 linchpin——从 \"one-benchmark curiosity\" 升级为\n\n    \"retrieval-task phenomenon confirmed on two independent benchmarks\"。\n\n    BoolQ/COPA gradient strengthens taxonomy without needing to be significant themselves。\n\n    Combined 9-benchmark dose-response plot（convergence strength vs retrieval demand）\n\n    成为 Claim 1 的 definitive visualization。'\n","numLines":752,"startLine":1,"totalLines":752}}}
