\n3. **Strengths** (bulleted, 4-6 items)\n4. **Weaknesses** (bulleted, 4-6 items, be specific and actionable)\n5. **Questions for authors** (3-5 items)\n6. **Missing experiments or coverage gaps** — compare against the experiment plan to identify what's missing or underrepresented\n7. **Minor issues** (formatting, clarity, missing details)\n8. **Scores**: Soundness (1-5), Excitement (1-5), Reproducibility (1-5), Overall Assessment (1-5, half-point), Confidence (1-5)\n\nBe rigorous but fair. This is a community analysis paper using public infrastructure — evaluate it as such, not as if it should produce new models or training recipes.","uuid":"45161e67-fe1f-44a1-bdf6-9e73374fee69","session_id":"e9550a7c-c680-4184-8420-886a108eb62d"}
